From 180c3d391241490e942cce3d355fea955c4d906d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: degas <degas@local>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 19:46:09 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Enable the SystemUI flashlight strength slider

The QS flashlight tile can open a dialog with a brightness slider, but the
code path is fused off: com.android.systemui.flashlight_strength defaults to
disabled and is read-only, so no runtime override can reach it.

degas reports android.flash.info.strengthMaximumLevel = 100 on both
flash-bearing cameras, which is what CameraManager.turnOnTorchWithStrengthLevel
needs, so the feature has something to talk to.
---
 .../flashlight_strength_flag_values.textproto               | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 release/aconfig/bp4a/com.android.systemui/flashlight_strength_flag_values.textproto

diff --git a/release/aconfig/bp4a/com.android.systemui/flashlight_strength_flag_values.textproto b/release/aconfig/bp4a/com.android.systemui/flashlight_strength_flag_values.textproto
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1ddd7bc
--- /dev/null
+++ b/release/aconfig/bp4a/com.android.systemui/flashlight_strength_flag_values.textproto
@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@
+flag_value {
+  package: "com.android.systemui"
+  name: "flashlight_strength"
+  state: ENABLED
+  permission: READ_ONLY
+}
-- 
2.55.0

